{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>YHWH will command the blessing with you in your storehouses.</b> For it is said (Job 22:28): ״וְתִגְזַר אֹמֶר וְיָקָם לָךְ״ — when the righteous man decrees a decree, the Holy One, blessed be He, consents through him, as in ״שֶׁמֶשׁ בְּגִבְעוֹן דּוֹם״ (Joshua 10:12), and as with Elijah who said: ״כַּד הַקֶּמַח לֹא תִכְלָה״ (I Kings 17:14), and in the Gemara (Ta'anit 25a) regarding Rabbi Ḥanina ben Dosa: where did the vinegar go, O your goats? — and many like these. Therefore it is said: ״יְצַו ה׳ אִתְּךָ אֶת הַבְּרָכָה״ — when you give command concerning the blessing, then YHWH will command with you and consent to the blessing and to your command." "And from the fact that it says ״בַּאֲסָמֶיךָ, וּבְכֹל מִשְׁלַח יָדֶךָ, וּבֵרַכְךָ בָּאָרֶץ״, hear from this that words, words did he teach — and each is a blessing in its own right. And perhaps they correspond to what is said (Proverbs 6:22): ״בְּהִתְהַלֶּכְךָ תַּנְחֶה אוֹתָךְ״ — in this world; ״בְּשָׁכְבְּךָ תִּשְׁמוֹר עָלֶיךָ״ — in the grave; ״וַהֲקִיצוֹתָ הִיא תְשִׂיחֶךָ״ — in the world to come (Avot 6:9). And when it says ״הַבְּרָכָה בַּאֲסָמֶיךָ״, it alludes to the world to come, which is hidden from the eye, for blessing is found not in a thing that is measured and counted but only in what is hidden from the eye (Bava Metzi'a 42a). They alluded by this that the success of this world is not the ultimate purpose of blessing, for all of it is a measured and counted thing that has a limit and a boundary and an end and is not eternal — except for the reward of the world to come, which eye has not seen; it is eternal and it is the essence, as it is written (Psalms 133:3): ״כְּטַל חֶרְמוֹן שֶׁיּוֹרֵד עַל הַרְרֵי צִיּוֹן״ etc. — that is the dew by which the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to revive the dead, and it descends upon the mountains of Zion, for there is the gate of heaven and the place of ascent for souls to the Garden of Eden. And it says ״כִּי שָׁם צִוָּה ה׳ אֶת הַבְּרָכָה חַיִּים עַד הָעוֹלָם״, for those life-years are eternal and everlasting; therefore there is the essence of the blessing — but not in a measured and counted thing which has an end and a limit. And concerning this blessing it says: ״יְצַו ה׳ אִתְּךָ אֶת הַבְּרָכָה בַּאֲסָמֶיךָ״ — in the world to come, which is hidden from the eye. And therefore it says ״אִתְּךָ״, for this acquisition is with you and cleaves to you, since the soul's persistence is not outside of it but rather the thing is always with it, accompanying it — not so the reward of this world, which is external to it, as the Rambam wrote (in Shemonah Perakim) that the acquisition of wealth is outside of man and does not cleave to him, but rather passes from hand to hand, for it is a wheel that turns in the world. And concerning it he said: ״וּבְכֹל מִשְׁלַח יָדֶךָ״, which is the reward of ״בְּהִתְהַלֶּכְךָ״ — in this world." "Afterward he mentioned the intermediate boundary, which is between these two boundaries, and that is ״בְּשָׁכְבְּךָ״ — in the grave, in the earth — for the dead of the land of Israel do not suffer the anguish of the grave's pounding and rolling through chambers, and they live first. And concerning this it says: ״וּבֵרַכְךָ בָּאָרֶץ״ — at the time of your lying down in the bosom of the earth which YHWH your Elohim gives you, for specifically the dead of the land of Israel are enabled in this. And after he mentioned the time of lying down in the earth, he mentioned the time of rising, and said: ״יְקִימְךָ ה׳ לוֹ לְעַם קָדוֹשׁ״, and this rising is in the manner spoken of (Deuteronomy 31:16): ״הִנְּךָ שׁוֹכֵב עִם אֲבוֹתֶיךָ וְקָם״ — that is, the rising of the future, as it is written (Isaiah 26:19): ״יִחְיוּ מֵתֶיךָ נְבֵלָתִי יְקוּמוּן הָקִיצוּ וְרַנְּנוּ שׁוֹכְנֵי עָפָר״ etc." "And if you would say that it is fitting to arrange these three times according to the order of their occurrence, in the manner that they are mentioned in the verse ״בְּהִתְהַלֶּכְךָ תַּנְחֶה אוֹתָךְ״ — then we can say that what it says, ״יְצַו ה׳ אִתְּךָ אֶת הַבְּרָכָה בַּאֲסָמֶיךָ וּבְכֹל מִשְׁלַח יָדֶךָ״, speaks of the reward of this world according to its plain sense; ״וּבֵרַכְךָ בָּאָרֶץ״ — that is, when you lie down in the grave; ״יְקִימְךָ ה׳ לוֹ״ — that is, at the time of the rising, in the world to come." "Another matter: ״בַּאֲסָמֶיךָ״ means storehouses of grain, and since the nature of storehouses is to be maintained by placing into them from the soil of that place, as Rashi explained on the verse ״שְׂדֵה הָעִיר אֲשֶׁר סְבִיבוֹתֶיהָ נָתַן בְּתוֹכָהּ״ (Genesis 41:48), therefore it says here: ״וּבֵרַכְךָ בָּאָרֶץ״ — by your placing from the earth into the storehouse, it will be maintained." "And as for what is said, ״יִפְתַּח ה׳ לְךָ אֶת אוֹצָרוֹ הַטּוֹב״ — this is that treasure which the Holy One, blessed be He, makes in heaven from the fear of HaShem that is within you, for it is His treasure, as it is written (Isaiah 33:6): ״יִרְאַת ה׳ הִיא אוֹצָרוֹ״, meaning that of the Holy One, blessed be He, as Rabbeinu Bachaye explained (Exodus 19:5), that every king makes a treasure and special possession from a thing that is not available in his hand at all times, such as precious stones — and so too, all is in the hands of heaven except the fear of heaven (Berakhot 33a). Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, makes a treasure from the fear of HaShem that is within you.\n\nAnd perhaps you might err and say that the Holy One, blessed be He, has some need for this treasure — therefore it says: ״יִפְתַּח ה׳ לְךָ אֶת אוֹצָרוֹ הַטּוֹב״ — He, blessed be He, has no need whatsoever for that treasure, for it is stored only for you, to give you from there all your needs and to sustain you from there. And the Holy One, blessed be He, does not hand over the key to this treasure to an intermediary; rather, the Holy One, blessed be He, Himself, in His glory, holds it in His hand, for this treasure is very precious to Him.\n\nAnd with this is settled what our Rabbis of blessed memory said in tractate Ta'anit (2a): three keys were not given into the hand of an intermediary — that of the womb, that of rains, and that of the resurrection of the dead. This is well for the womb and resurrection, for He, blessed be He, is the source of life for all who are born and for the time of resurrection; but rains — how are they different from all other things? Rather, because their source is from that treasure of the fear of HaShem, as it is written: ״יִפְתַּח לְךָ אֶת אוֹצָרוֹ הַטּוֹב אֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם לָתֵת מְטַר אַרְצְךָ״, for the rain is stored in that chamber where the treasure of HaShem is."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {5 "The citation 'רַבֵּינוּ בְּחַיֵּי' is resolved as Rabbeinu Bachaye, referring to Bachaye ben Asher on Exodus 19:5; the tractate reference 'תַּעֲנִית (ב.)' is normalized to Ta'anit 2a based on the well-known passage there about the three keys."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:14:45.054375129Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}